 "visual": "\"1898\". Warships to Manila. Hawaii as the stepping stone. US flag rises.",
 "texto": "Then came the Spanish-American War. American warships were heading to the Philippines, and Hawaii was the perfect stop on the way. In 1898, Congress annexed the islands with a simple resolution. No treaty. No vote by the people who lived there. On August 12th, 1898, the Hawaiian flag was lowered at Iolani Palace and the American flag went up. Many Hawaiians stayed home that day, refusing to watch.",
